('9b761332-d589-50e9-b57e-91588af85b3b'::uuid,'c906fb73-66a3-5477-8732-349b15f6e5c4'::uuid,'v0.9 consolidated draft','> **Reviewer note added when this draft was loaded into the platform (31 Oct 2026).** Section 1.1 quotes the workbook Dashboard as last saved (Part A 2.38, Part B 1.66, Part C 1.29, combined 2.18, mandatory compliance 39.4%, 30 High gaps). Those cached values were never recalculated after the 30 Oct edits. Recalculating from the workbook''s own scores gives Part A 2.35, Part B 1.47, Part C 1.26, combined 2.04, mandatory compliance 34.2% and 37 High gaps. Under the IAT evidence rule (interviews alone cannot raise a score above 2), A1.4 and A1.7 also rest on FGD self-scores only. Update the figures and the A1 table after the workbook is re-scored and recalculated.
